* aldb commands

Implement in the aldb-mode an exhaustive set of commands and keybindings.
They will be mostly useful in the *aldb-stack* buffer.


You may also look at the sources of slime.el for inspiration
~/quicklisp/dists/quicklisp/software/slime-v2.32/slime.el

Command arguments are read from the minibuffer ; parsing may be deferred to aldo.

** Commands to examine the selected frame:

| keys | command with parameters)                 | description                                                                 |
|------+------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| t    | (aldb-toggle-details &optional ON)       | displays the locals below the line of the frame in the *aldb-stack* buffer. |
| v    | (aldb-show-source)                       | switch too the source buffer in another window                            |
| e    | (aldb-eval-in-frame FRAME STRING)        | evaluates in frame                                                          |
| d    | (aldb-pprint-eval-in-frame FRAME STRING) | evaluates in frame, pretty-print the result.                                |
| i    | (aldb-inspect-in-frame STRING)           | inspect in another window                                                   |


** Commands to invoke restarts:

We don't have restarts, but a few aldo commands.
Note, when we exit from aldo (quit to toplevel, continue, finish, etc), in emacs  revert to windows as they were before aldb.
For a step into or step over, don't change the windows (we should be back soon).


| keys | command with parameters) | description                                           |
|------+--------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------|
| q    | (aldb-quit)              | quit aldo to toplevel.                                |
| c    | (aldb-continue)          | invoke the aldo continue command.                     |

** Commands to navigate frames:

| keys | command with parameters)      | description                                                                                            |
|------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| n    | (aldb-down)                   | select the next frame                                                                                  |
| p    | (aldb-up)                     | select the previous frame                                                                              |
| M-n  | (aldb-details-down)           | down, with details (close the locals of the current frame, move to next frame, and open the locals).   |
| M-p  | (aldb-details-up)             | up, with details (close the locals of the current frame, move to previous frame, and open the locals). |
| <    | (aldb-beginning-of-backtrace) | beginning of backtrace                                                                                 |
| >    | (aldb-end-of-backtrace)       | end of backtrace                                                                                       |


** Miscellaneous commands:

| keys | command with parameters)        | description                                             |
|------+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------|
| r    | (aldb-restart-frame)            | restart frame: jump to the beginning of the function    |
| R    | (aldb-return-from-frame STRING) | input a value to return with the aldo return command.   |
| s, i | (aldb-step-in)                  | step in                                                 |
| S, o | (aldb-step-out)                 | step out                                                |
| B    | (aldb-break-with-aldo)          | switch to native debugger (aldo)                |
| A    | (aldb-break-with-aldo)          | switch to system debugger (aldo)                    |
| :    | (aldb-interactive-eval STRING)  | Read and evaluate STRING and print value in minibuffer. |
| C    | (aldb-inspect-error)            | redisplay error message                                 |

** Full list of commands:


| Key         | Command                        |
|-------------+--------------------------------|
| TAB         | aldb-cycle                   |
| RET         | aldb-default-action            |
| C-y         | aldb-insert-frame-call-to-repl |
| :           | aldb-eval-in-frame             |
| <           | aldb-beginning-of-backtrace    |
| >           | aldb-end-of-backtrace          |
| A           | aldb-break-with-aldo           |
| B           | aldb-break-with-aldo           |
| C           | aldb-inspect-error             |
| I           | aldb-invoke-restart-by-name    |
| R           | aldb-return-from-frame         |
| a           | aldb-abort                     |
| b           | aldb-break                     |
| c           | aldb-continue                  |
| d           | aldb-pprint-eval-in-frame      |
| e           | aldb-eval-in-frame             |
| i           | aldb-inspect-in-frame          |
| n           | aldb-down                      |
| o           | aldb-out                       |
| p           | aldb-up                        |
| q           | aldb-quit                      |
| r           | aldb-restart-frame             |
| s           | aldb-step-in                   |
| i           | aldb-step-in                   |
| o           | aldb-step-over                 |
| t           | aldb-toggle-details            |
| v           | aldb-show-source               |
| x           | aldb-step-over                 |
| h           | describe-mode                  |
| <return>    | aldb-default-action            |
| M-n         | aldb-details-down              |
| M-p         | aldb-details-up                |
|-------------+--------------------------------|
| C-c C-d C-g | alref-lookup                   |
| C-c C-d g   | alref-lookup                   |
| C-c C-d a   | alref-apropos                  |
| C-c C-d C-a | alref-apropos                  |
|-------------+--------------------------------|

** Notes

- the default action on a stack frame line is to do: aldb-toggle-details
- the default action on a local binding line is to do aldb-inspect-in-frame

aldb-cycle goes from *aldb-stack* to *aldb* and vice-versa.

If some aldo commands are not accessible from these aldb commands,
signals them and propose an aldb command to invoke it.

